<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Omabook releases</title><id>https://jellespijker.github.io/omabook/</id><link href="https://jellespijker.github.io/omabook/releases.xml" rel="self"/><link href="https://jellespijker.github.io/omabook/"/><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00Z</updated><entry><title>Omabook 0.4.0</title><id>https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.4.0</id><link href="https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.4.0"/><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00Z</updated><summary>Omabook listens: notes dictated, questions asked by voice and answered aloud, what to do said while reading, and recordings written out to read and search. Ink goes in the margins and between the lines of every book, the margin folds away to dots, and each row of the AI page can be tested and finds a missing model. The package now needs `qt6-websockets`, and `ffmpeg` for recordings in other formats than WAV and Opus.</summary></entry><entry><title>Omabook 0.3.2</title><id>https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.2</id><link href="https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.2"/><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00Z</updated><summary>0.3.1&#x27;s one-time library upgrade could take a book&#x27;s own identifiers away; this one keeps them. Upgrade to 0.3.2, not 0.3.1.</summary></entry><entry><title>Omabook 0.3.1</title><id>https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.1</id><link href="https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.1"/><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00Z</updated><summary>### Fixed</summary></entry><entry><title>Omabook 0.3.0</title><id>https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.0</id><link href="https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.3.0"/><updated>2026-11-22T00:00:00Z</updated><summary>### Added</summary></entry><entry><title>Omabook 0.2.2</title><id>https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/tag/v0.2.2</id><link href="https://github.com/jellespijker/omabook/releases/t